meta {
  name: supervisor /skill park
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

post {
  url: {{supervisorUrl}}/skill
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "skill": "park",
    "mission_id": "{{mission}}",
    "args_json": "{\"arm\": \"{{arm}}\"}"
  }
}

docs {
  park is a skill, not an MCP tool: it is the same judgement the ROS service makes, reached over the
  supervisor's HTTP port. It writes the measured parked pose for that arm (no conversion: those numbers are in
  the degrees the arm reports), needs torque on, and the reply carries accepted, reason and ticket.

  Two repeated parks land within 0.00 deg of each other — the reason the skill exists instead of folding by hand.
}
